Preheat your oven to 400ºF.

If you’re using @saffron{1}(pinch) or @turmeric{}, combine with @heavy cream{1/4%cup} and set aside.

In a blender, make a marinade by adding @fried onions{1%tbsp}, @greek yogurt{1%cup}, @garlic{6%cloves}(peeled), @ginger{1 inch}(peeled and sliced), @ground cumin{1%tbsp}, @cilantro{1/2 bunch}(), @red chili powder{1-2%tsp} (and @jalapeño{1}(optional, if you are ok with spice)) and @salt{=2%tsp}. Puree until smooth, then combine with @chicken thighs{2 lbs}(bone in skin on) and marinate for at least ~{30%minutes} (longer is better).

In a large #oven-proof pot{2.5qt dutch oven}, bring @water{4%cups} and a good pinch of @salt{} to a boil. When the water is boiling, add @basmati rice{2%cups} and cook for ~{5%minutes}, then drain into a fine mesh sieve. If you don’t have a sieve, try to carefully drain as well as you can and transfer to a bowl.

In your now empty dutch oven, put down 1 layer of chicken, then cover with half the rice, then half the cream, and half the @onion{1/4}(diced). Repeat again with the remaining chicken, rice, cream, and onions.

Cover and bake for ~{1 hour}, then remove from the oven and allow to steam an extra ~{15%minutes} before opening the lid. Mix well and serve with extra @fried onions{}, @greek yogurt{}, and chopped flat leaf @parsley{} or @cilantro{}.
